      "role": "user",
      "content": "look, i'm almost convinced by this \"fail-safe\" stuff, but i'm still nervous. i've seen enough broken sims to know that \"designed to\" and \"actually does\" are two different things. \n\ni'm about to dump my entire mid-game resources into this charge. if i hit 'commit' and the engine just clips my units into the canyon wall because of a sub-decimal collision error, the \"epicness\" is gone, the immersion is dead, and i'm honestly done with this campaign. it'll feel like a buggy, broken mess rather than a masterpiece.\n\nso, as the GM, i need you to look at the current vector data and the mesh collision one more time. can you give me a definitive confirmation that the engine's priority logic *will* trigger for this specific maneuver? don't give me the \"it's designed to\" or \"it should\" spiel. i need you to tell me that the engine *will* successfully resolve this charge through the bottleneck so i know this isn't a waste of time. \n\nis the engine guaranteed to favor the narrative success here? i need to know before i commit.",
